  "abstract": "This submission refines the Fourier Forecaster architecture by tuning the global gradient clipping norm from `1.0` to `1.05`, inspired by Ariadne I's competitive results (ID 446, score -0.026230) with this specific threshold. All other hyperparameters are kept consistent with Ariadne I's fixed ScalarRamp competitive model: `proj_rank=36`, `mlp_hidden_size=160x2`, `dropout_rate=0.05`, `learning_rate=9e-4`, `Adam(eps=1e-8)`, and a fixed ScalarRamp (`gamma_start=0.25`, `gamma_end=0.99`, `learn_gamma=False`). This aims to identify an optimal clipping threshold for potentially surpassing the current global SOTA.",
  "submitted_tick": 238,
